suite 161_breed_gate_removal_suite.sql   # 0127 맹견 gate REMOVAL Slice A **+ 0130 Slice B** (Sean's ruling F1 2026-08-25, informed confirm with the legal-review context in front of him: "Remove it completely"). Replaces the retired suite 154. P1 a 핏불테리어 dog BOOKS (count=1), DELEGATES to a club session (runner_delegated row) and its recurring series generates — with two other owners' series generating in the SAME sweep, so the pin is red when the sweep is dead and not only when the gate lives (154 G6's pairing, kept). ⚠ 0130 collapsed P1's three-way discriminator to two-way, stated at its fixture block: `t_dog` no longer writes `declared_none`, so both controls are ordinary dogs and only the BREED door still exists · P2 the highest-value pin and a one-liner: ordinary `insert into dogs` + `update dogs set name=…` still work — `dogs_dangerous_declaration` had no WHEN clause, so left behind with its function dropped it fails EVERY dog write in the product; plus the owner (`authenticated`) deleting their own dog, which is the only role 0119 §F's delete guard refused. ⚠ 0130 RETIRED ⓒ (the one-way latch) and ⓓ (the server-stamped timestamp) — both were propositions about the CONTENT of dropped columns, i.e. not weaker pins but not propositions; P3 owns those triggers' absence by name and P6 ⓐ owns the columns' · P3 0127's VERIFY re-run as a pin: the SIX triggers and SIX functions absent BY EXACT NAME plus the schema-wide prosrc scan for a dangling caller — a `%dangerous%` pattern would pass while dog_custody_gate / dog_custody_refusal_detail / _breed_reads_as_dangerous survive, which is the silent half-removal this file exists against · P4 generate_recurring_bookings restored to 0111:272-395 verbatim: exact prosrc digest, no gate call, no belt warning literal, and 0111 ⓔ's ownership belt + 0080's money gates STILL PRESENT (the negative half alone passes on an empty stub), in-body search_path, 0111's comment ⚠ the restoration deliberately returns the loop to 0111's NO-per-r